WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:06.299
Hollywood lined up plenty of successful horror
projects in 2017, from Jordan Peele's breakthrough

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:11.020
hit Get Out to the revival of Stephen King's
IT to the Groundhog's Day redux Happy Death

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:11.540
Day.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:16.760
Looking ahead to 2018, there are already quite
a few flicks poised to satisfy fright fans

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:21.400
-- from fact-based stories to supernatural
scares and the reemergence of at least one

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:26.900
classic character, the future looks very dark
indeed, in the best possible way.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.620
Insidious: The Last Key

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:35.580
Demonologist Elise Rainier has been a staple
of the Insidious series despite meeting her

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:36.100
end in the first entry.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.780
After appearing only as a spirit in the second
film, the character was given the full prequel

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:45.260
treatment with Insidious: Chapter 3, which
focused on one of the "case files" from her

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:49.340
early days and explored how she came to meet
partners Specs and Tucker.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:54.990
Now, Insidious: The Last Key is expected to
return to Elise's story, picking up where

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:59.280
Chapter 3 left off -- only this time, she's
investigating a haunting of her own family

00:00:59.280 --> 00:00:59.780
home.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.780
From the looks of the film's trailer, it's
going to be just as chock full of jump scares

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:07.060
as the rest of the series when it hits theaters
January 5th.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.100
Day of the Dead: Bloodline

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:16.020
Reimagining George is quite a tricky proposition,
especially when we're talking about 1985's

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:19.571
Day of the Dead, which is one of the more
controversial entries in the Night of the

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:23.340
Living Dead series, for its unprecedented
level of violence and gore.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:28.180
Spanish writer/director Hèctor Hernández
Vicens will attempt to make it work, though,

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:30.980
with a loose adaptation titled Day of the
Dead: Bloodline.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:38.100
Vicens made a few waves in 2015 with his controversial
but well-received The Corpse of Anna Fritz,

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.300
but the bodies should be a little livelier
this time around.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:46.460
The new Day will drop on January 5th, with
a simultaneous theatrical and Digital HD release.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.680
Strangers: Prey at Night

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:55.020
The Strangers was a surprise hit in 2008 thanks
to its slow-burn brutality and subversion

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.440
of certain plot expectations.

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:59.500
"Why are you doing this to us?"

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.540
"Because you were home."

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:08.340
And even though the first sequel was announced
shortly after the film's release, it's taken

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.320
the better part of a decade to make it happen.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:15.340
The new film takes place at a trailer park
in the middle of nowhere during a power outage

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:19.440
and features Christina Hendricks as the head
of a family whose road trip takes an unfortunate

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:19.960
turn.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:24.040
Count on this one to creep everyone out when
it lands in theaters March 9th.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:25.840
The New Mutants

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:31.100
Writer-director Josh Boone is probably best
known for his adaptation of the romantic drama

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:34.240
novel The Fault in Our Stars, but not for
long.

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:39.960
A longtime fan of the Marvel comic book series
The New Mutants, Boone apparently blew away

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:45.240
Fox executives with his pitch for a film adaptation
of the property—a straight-up horror movie

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:50.520
based on a particularly dark run by legendary
writer Chris Claremont and artist Bill Sienkiewicz.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:55.560
Unlike other Marvel mutant films, The New
Mutants is much less sci-fi centric and much

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.080
more focused on the fright factors of its
characters.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:02.820
And with a cast that includes Split and The
Witch alum Anya Taylor-Joy alongside Game

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:07.280
of Thrones' Maisie Williams and Stranger Things
star Charlie Heaton, The New Mutants should

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:10.080
be one to watch when it hits theaters on April
13th.

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:12.000
Slender Man

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:17.620
Based on one of the notorious internet memes
of all time, Slender Man is expected to give

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:21.840
cinematic life to the viral villain that has
stalked the Web since 2009.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:27.560
The character was first born when a Photoshop
contest produced a picture of the tall, thin,

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.200
faceless stalker of hapless children.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:34.440
The forum poster who made the image, Eric
Knudsen, even has a writing credit on the

00:03:34.459 --> 00:03:39.579
film under his forum handle "Victor Surge"—a
development he probably didn't expect when

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:42.100
he set out to freak out a few people with
his Photoshop skills.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:46.100
Sony/Screen Gems has slated Slender Man for
release on May 18th.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.440
The Purge: The Island

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:54.379
The ending of 2016's The Purge: Election Year
seemed to shut the door pretty firmly on the

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.400
idea of more sequels.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:04:01.019
But the series has garnered such a huge fan
base that The Purge: The Island is now expected

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:03.320
to explore the beginnings of the title slaughterfest.

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:08.080
Creator James DeMonaco told Vulture that it's
set in Staten Island, New York, where the

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:13.880
first experimental purge took place, and that
it'll begin with people being paid to participate,

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:18.220
which incentivizes very poor people to try
their luck at surviving the night of mayhem

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:20.620
and violence, as DeMonaco said:

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:26.300
"...so you see the inception of how grotesque
the idea of the Purge is, and the manipulation

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.200
upon the society."

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.780
The Purge: The Island is set to hit theaters
on July 4th.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:32.360
The Nun

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:37.760
The series that New Line is now officially
calling the "Conjuring Universe" scored another

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:43.550
box office hit with Annabelle: Creation, a
pre-prequel exploring the origins of the sinister

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:48.760
doll from The Conjuring, pushing the series'
worldwide box office take up over the $1 billion

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:49.280
mark.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:55.020
Hitting those kinds of numbers can only ensure
plenty more films in the pipeline, and first

00:04:55.020 --> 00:05:00.190
up is another spinoff—The Nun, which will
add some backstory to one of Conjuring 2's

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:01.000
most terrifying characters.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:07.080
The story will center on the character's backstory
as a Romanian nun who ended her own life,

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:11.889
and the film will star Taissa Farmiga in the
lead, with Bonnie Aarons reprising her role

00:05:11.889 --> 00:05:13.480
as the demonic nun Valak.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:17.540
The Nun will return to scare your pants off
on July 13th.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.300
The House with a Clock in Its Walls

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:26.100
It sounds like a rather Harry Potter-esque
premise: a 10-year-old boy moves in with an

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:31.580
eccentric uncle, only to find his house full
of secret passageways and strange and creepy

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:32.100
goings-on.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:37.220
It's eventually revealed that his uncle is
a warlock, a witch lives next door, and the

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:40.120
house is a conduit for weird black magic rituals.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:41.460
But J.K.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:47.240
Rowling won't be calling her lawyers anytime
soon—this is the plot of the 1973 gothic

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:51.660
horror novel The House With a Clock In Its
Walls, and an adaptation is forthcoming with

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.240
some serious talent on board.

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:58.560
Notorious gore-master Eli Roth will direct
a cast that includes Kyle MacLachlan along

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:02.400
with Cate Blanchett, Jack Black and Renee
Elise Goldsberry.

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:07.780
This has out-of-left-field horror smash written
all over it, as long as Roth can keep his

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:09.860
more exploitative tendencies in check.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:12.680
Look for this film to hit theaters on September
21st.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:15.660
Something in the Dark

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:21.139
This tech-based thriller has a unique premise:
a blind woman has her sight restored by a

00:06:21.139 --> 00:06:26.580
pair of high-tech eyeglasses, but unfortunately,
her vision may now be a little better than

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:29.100
she bargained for, as she can now see ghosts.

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:33.470
Further complicating matters, they look just
like normal people, which means she can't

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:35.440
tell the difference between the dead and the
living.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:40.700
Even worse, she begins to suspect that a lurking
entity she keeps seeing might be coming for

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:41.200
her.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:46.380
The film is expected to be dialogue-free,
but if the super-creepy trailer by is any

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:50.380
indication, Something in the Dark could be
a breakout horror hit when it's released on

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:51.840
October 15th.

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:53.460
Halloween

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:58.680
The Halloween reboot series by Rob Zombie
was so-so at best, but with funnyman Danny

00:06:58.699 --> 00:07:03.009
McBride and producer David Gordon Green coming
together to work on the concept for the new

00:07:03.009 --> 00:07:06.320
film, the new version of the holiday favorite
might just work.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:12.039
The duo pitched directly to original director/co-writer
John Carpenter, and Carpenter's reaction was

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:14.060
enough to get any fan's heart racing.

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:15.380
He wrote on Facebook:

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:20.280
"David and Danny both came to my office recently
with Jason Blum [rhymes with plum] and shared

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:22.840
their vision for the new movie and…WOW.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:24.060
They get it.

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:25.500
I think you're gonna dig it."

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.320
McBride has since explained his vision like
so:

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:34.520
"The first Halloween just works on such a
gut level of there's someone who's escaped

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.760
an asylum and he's in this town."

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:38.220
"That's what we were wanting to do with this."

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:43.340
Rather than being a reboot, it's expected
to be more of a sequel to the original film.

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:47.820
Miramax will release the film on October 19th,
just in time for the scariest night of the

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:48.320
year.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:50.360
Nosferatu

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:57.080
The Witch is widely considered to be among
the scariest films of 2015, a unique and ambitious

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:01.540
picture that was the directorial debut of
production designer-turned-director Robert

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:02.060
Eggers.

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:07.360
The film grossed ten times its budget, and
for his follow-up, Eggers isn't scaling back

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:08.500
on his ambition.

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:15.479
He'll be helming a remake of the seminal 1922
horror classic Nosferatu, an undertaking only

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:20.800
attempted once before—in 1979, by acclaimed
German filmmaker Werner Herzog.

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:26.700
Eggers' gift for atmosphere should serve him
well on this project, which even he admits

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:27.240
is daunting.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:31.460
Briefly tempted to table the remake, he told
Collider that he reconsidered:

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:37.719
"It feels ugly and blasphemous and egomaniacal
and disgusting for a filmmaker in my place

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:39.420
to do Nosferatu next.

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:43.600
I was really planning on waiting a while,
but that's how fate shook out."

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:48.760
It's safe to say the remake is in very good
hands—and if The Witch is any indication,

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:51.600
fans might be in for the creepiest vampire
flick in years.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:53.700
Deep Blue Sea 2

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:58.200
The 1999 cult classic Deep Blue Sea is a film
that has everything.

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:04.500
There's giant mutant sharks, a Bible-quoting
LL Cool J and his parrot sidekick, and a thundering

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:09.280
Samuel L. Jackson monologue that ends in the
most hilarious and inevitable way possible.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:14.320
"We're going to pull together, and we're going
to find a way to get out of here."

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.240
"First, we're going to seal off this hole!"

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:23.680
It's one of the most fun popcorn movies of
the '90s, and it even turned a decent profit,

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:27.180
but plans for a sequel have repeatedly fallen
through—until now.

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:32.980
The Syfy Channel, purveyors of the finest
shark-based schlock of this or any age, reportedly

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:36.040
took on shooting the long-awaited Deep Blue
Sea 2.

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:41.140
It may not be getting a theatrical release,
but Syfy seems like a good home for the project,

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:45.680
which will hopefully live up to the fantastically
cheesy legacy of its predecessor.

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:48.340
​Puppet Master: The Littlest Reich

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:54.220
Puppet Master didn't seem destined to crank
out sequel after sequel when it made its direct-to-video

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:58.960
debut in 1989, but the franchise has proved
to have remarkable staying power.

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:04.740
Focusing on evil puppets animated by an ancient
curse and the man who created them, the film

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:07.540
has already spawned no fewer than ten sequels.

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:13.860
This year's Puppet Master: Axis Termination—the
first installment since 2012—debuted in

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:19.320
September on Amazon, but the team behind next
year's The Littlest Reich have assembled enough

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:22.620
talent that fans are crossing their fingers
hoping for a theatrical release.

00:10:23.570 --> 00:10:29.560
The film will star stone-faced veteran actor
Udo Kier as the deranged puppet maker Toulon,

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:32.360
and genre queen Barbara Crampton will also
make an appearance.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:37.060
Most of the action is expected to take place
at a convention, where killer puppets will

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:42.100
run amok, and producers have promised a bloody
good time with plenty of practical gore effects

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:44.100
when the film arrives sometime next year.

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:47.260
Piranha JPN: Teeth of the Piranha

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:53.300
1978's Piranha has the distinction of being
hands-down the best Jaws rip-off in a sea

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:58.529
of ripoffs, and it also launched the career
of director Joe Dante in much the same way

00:10:58.529 --> 00:11:02.920
that its less-loved sequel gave a boost to
future Hollywood titan James Cameron.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:08.950
The modern reboot series, which began with
2010's Piranha 3D, has nobly carried on the

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:14.240
tradition of delivering maximum cheese along
with copious amounts of gore and bare bodies.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:19.720
So, we're pleased to report that the next
installment—titled Piranha JPN: Teeth of

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:21.900
the Piranha—is expected to drop sometime
next year.

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:23.680
Polaroid

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:28.400
Although unrelated issues with The Weinstein
Company and Dimension Films have caused delays

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:33.120
in the release of Polaroid, a supernatural
thriller originally slated for a Thanksgiving

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:38.620
2017 release, the film still looks bonkers
enough to survive the executive changes underway

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:39.320
at the studio.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:44.160
First-time feature director Lars Klevberg
adapts from his own short film, telling the

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:49.380
story of a teenage loner who discovers an
old Polaroid camera in a mysterious store.

00:11:49.780 --> 00:11:54.440
The budding photo enthusiast soon finds that
anybody she takes a picture of is in line

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:57.580
for a horrific death at the hands of some
malevolent force.

00:11:58.029 --> 00:12:02.660
While the premise might seem a touch familiar—or,
specifically, like a mashup of The Ring and

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:07.680
Final Destination—Klevberg's film won Best
Short and Best Cinematography awards at the

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:13.220
prestigious Los Angeles Horror Competition,
and all signs in the trailer point to a stylishly

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:14.500
shot and creepy flick.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:15.700
Thanks for watching!

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:18.540
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:21.000
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

